From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: media: sunxi: sun50i-g2d: clock both engines and self-test the
 hardware at probe

On the Orange Pi Zero2 every mixer job timed out with the finish
interrupt register reading back 0, even its enable bit, which the
driver had just written: the mixer never started, and its registers
did not seem to hold the values written to them. The TOP registers
(IP version 0x01010100) do respond.

Follow the BSP's power-up sequence more closely: release the reset
before the clocks are enabled, gate on and release both engines in the
TOP block (0x3, as g2d_bsp_open() does) rather than the mixer alone,
pulse the reset of both engines before every job (g2d_bsp_reset()),
and set the start bit with a read-modify-write of the control
register.

So that a single boot tells which part of the block is alive, add a
probe-time self-test that only logs: a write/read-back of a few mixer
and rotation engine registers with the capability fields of the IP
version register, then a 16x16 copy through the mixer and through the
rotation engine, each waited for on its finish interrupt and checked
against the source. The rotation engine's finish interrupt is handled
for that. The job timeout message now also prints the control, TOP and
layer registers and the interrupt count.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---

